--   **The call of `expPosP`.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegILSrc7`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.Src.callB_sp (s0 : IState HS) (F : Fin HS → List ℤ) {e16 e17 e18 e27 : Ex HS}
--       {n k jj σ A : ℕ} (hA : 2 ≤ A) (c16 : CIn s0 F A e16 n) (c17 : CIn s0 F A e17 k)
--       (c18 : CIn s0 F A e18 jj) (c27 : CIn s0 F A e27 σ) (hvA : |expPos n k jj σ| ≤ 2 ^ A) :
--       Sp (callB e16 e17 e18 e27) (encK s0 F) (encK s0 (update F 44 (expPos n k jj σ :: F 44)))
--         ((e16.size + e17.size + e18.size + e27.size + 12) * uC A DD +
--           expPosCost n (A * DD + 1) (A * DD + 1) σ)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, source-table producers, part 7: a call of `expPosP`
--
--   `callB e16 e17 e18 e27`: push the four inputs on `16, 17, 18, 27`, run the library program
--   `expPosP` (`NLogN`, output on `19`), push its result on `44`, pop `19, 27, 18, 17, 16`.
--   `callB_sp`: on `encK s0 F`, with the expressions' registers outside `16, 17, 18, 19, 27, 44`, the
--   result is `update F 44 (expPos n k j σ :: F 44)`; every other stack (including `16–19, 27`) is
--   unchanged.
